### Step 10 — Full-win record card (build second)

**Trigger rule:** record card appears only on **full win** — last stage of **level 5** cleared — **not** on intermediate stage clears, **not** after levels 1–4, **not** on game over (lose).

**Hook point:** `advanceAfterStars()` when `isLastStage && level >= MAX_LEVEL`. Today that branch sets `won` + `gameOver` immediately. New flow: stars dismiss → **record card** → user saves → play again.

**Levels 1–4:** unchanged — last stage cleared → auto-advance to next level (no record card).

**Layout (card over dim overlay; replaces today’s full-win tap-to-restart card):**
- Title: full win (`recordCard.title` or `strings.gameOver.titleWin`)
- **Final run score** (large) — cumulative `score` across all 5 levels
- **3-letter initials** — A–Z, max 3; pre-fill from `playerInitials`
- **Save** — `saveLeaderboardEntry(initials, score)` + persist `playerInitials`; show rank (`recordCard.rank`)
- **Play again** — `restartFromLevelOne()` (allow skip save → play again)

**Sequence:** stage goal met → stars (~1.5s) → stars dismiss → **record card** → Save (rank feedback) → play again

**Hook / state (`useCandyBreak.ts`):**
- `recordCardPending: boolean` — set when level 5 last stage clears; cleared after dismiss
- `saveRunToLeaderboard(initials: string): Promise<number>` — delegates to `leaderboard.ts`; returns rank
- `dismissRecordCard(): void` — `restartFromLevelOne()` or return to intro
- Gate: do not set `won`/`gameOver` until record card dismissed

**Record card + leaderboard link:** after Save, optional “View board” reuses `LeaderboardView` with `highlightRank`.

**i18n:** `recordCard.title`, `recordCard.score`, `recordCard.initialsLabel`, `recordCard.save`, `recordCard.playAgain`, `recordCard.rank`, `recordCard.viewBoard`

**Files (step 10 slice):**
1. `src/utils/leaderboard.ts` — complete `saveLeaderboardEntry` + migration from `bestScore`
2. `src/hooks/useCandyBreak.ts` — full-win gate + save API + `dismissRecordCard`
3. `src/components/RecordCardOverlay.tsx` — initials + save + play again
4. `App.tsx` — wire overlay when `recordCardPending`
5. `src/i18n/types.ts`, `translations.ts` — record card strings

**HUD (optional, later):** keep `bestScore` or derive from `leaderboard[0].score` — avoid two sources of truth after migration.

